$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-Benzyl-6-endo-(trimethylsilyl)oxy-6-exo-trifluoromethyl-3-azabicyclo[3.1.1]heptane
(9). Dry CsF (0.6 g, 4.0 mmol) was added to the solution of ketone 1 (2.0
g, 9.9 mmol) in dry THF (50 mL), and the formed suspension was cooled to
-5 °C. CF3 TMS (2.0 g, 14.1 mmol) was slowly added, and the reaction
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 16 h. Evaporation of the
solvent in vacuum provided a residue, which was treated with hot hexane.
Insoluble material was filtered off, and the organic phase was evaporated
in vacuum to give product 9 (3.4 g, 9.9 mmol, 100% yield) as pale yellow
liquid. It was used in the next step without additional purification. 1H
NMR (500 MHz; CDCl3; Me4Si), δ: 0.27 (9H, s, Si(CH3) 3), 1.98 (1H, m, CHH
of cyclobutane), 2.16 (1H, d, 2JH-H = 10.5 Hz, CHH of cyclobutane), 2.65
(2H, broad s, CH of cyclobutane), 2.85 (2H, d, J= 9.8 Hz, NCHH), 3.15
(2H, d, J= 8.6 Hz, NCHH), 3.75 (2H, s, NCH2Ph), 7.28-7.40 (5H, m, Ph).
13C NMR (125 MHz; CDCl3; Me4Si), δ: 1.59 (s, Si(CH3) 3), 20.20 (q, 4 JC-F
= 4.5 Hz, CH2 of cyclobutane), 39.56 (s, CH of cyclobutane), 50.88 (s,
PhCH2NCH2), 59.69 (s, NCH2Ph), 77.54 (q, 2 JC-F = 28.0 Hz, C-CF3), 126.77
(q, 1 JC-F = 284.7 Hz, CF3), 126.83 (s, CH, Ph), 128.21 (s, CH, Ph),
128.54 (s, CH, Ph), 139.43 (s, quat-C, Ph). MS (m/z): 343.
