$DATUM tert- Butyl 3-amino-4-(2,2,2-trifluoro-1-hydroxyethyl)benzoate (10). To a
stirred solution of the aldehyde 9 (4.0 g, 15.9 mmol) containing a
catalytic amount of dry CsF (~10 mg) in DME (53 mL) at 0 °C was added a
solution of TMSCF3 (8.0 mL, 2 M in THF, 15.9 mmol) under an argon
atmosphere. After being stirred for 5 h at room temperature, the reaction
mixture was treated with 10% HCl (30 mL) and diluted with EtOAc (30 mL).
Extractive workup and purification by column chromatography (EtOAc/Hexane
= 1/9) afforded the corresponding alcohol 10 as a yellowish solid (5.1 g,
100%). R f = 0.50 (EtOAc/Hexane = 1/4); mp 101.3 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 8.5 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 8.2 (dd, J = 8.2 and 1.5 Hz, 1H), 8.1
(d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 6.3 – 6.2 (m, 1H), 4.5 (d, J = 4.6 Hz, 1H), 1.6 (s,
9H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 164.4, 148.9, 134.5, 134.4, 133.7, 130.5,
126.3, 129.9, 126.1, 122.4, 118.7 [q, J = 277.5 Hz (coupled with F),
−CF3], 84.3, 67.8, 67.4, 67.0, 66.5 [q, J = 30.0Hz (coupled with F),
−C(OH)CF3] 28.6; 19F NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ −1.60, −1.62 (The -CF3 group
can have pseudo-equatorial and –axial position owing to intramolecular
H-bonding); HRMS (FAB) m/z for C13H15F3NO5 (M + H+) calcd 322.0902, found
322.0905.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Selective Colorimetric Sensing of Anions in Aqueous Media through
Reversible Covalent Bonding
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
