$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Fe-Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of
Aldehydes/Ketones. A 5 mM stock solution of TBA[Fe] (10.3 mg, 0.025 mmol)
and DMAP (3.05 mg, 0.025 mmol) in anhydrous THF (5 mL) was prepared in a
flame-dried Schlenk tube. Anhydrous THF (0.5 mL) and the stock solution
(1.5 mL, 0.0075 mmol, 0.75 mol % TBAFe and DMAP) were added to a
flame-dried Schlenk tube. The appropriate aldehyde (1.00 mmol, 1 equiv)
and TMS-CF3 (296 μL, 2.00 mmol, 2 equiv) were added under an atmosphere
of N2, and the mixture was stirred for 14 h at 30°C. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure, and the residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel as indicated below to afford the
trifluoromethylated silyl ethers 4-24.
Trimethyl(2,2,2-trifluoro-1-(4-methoxyphenyl)ethoxy)silane (4).82 The
title compound was purified by chromatography on silica gel with PE/EtOAc
50/1 (v/v) as eluent, 4 as a colorless oil (241 mg, 92% yield). Rf = 0.45
(PE/EtOAc 50/1 (v/v)); 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) 7.37 (d, J = 9.0
Hz, 2H), 6.90 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 4.87 (q, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 3.82 (s,
3H), 0.11 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (63 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) 160.1 (C), 128.8 (CH),
127.5 (C), 124.3 (q, J = 283.0 Hz, C), 113.7 (CH), 72.9 (q, J = 32.0 Hz,
CH), 55.2 (CH3), 0.3 (CH3); 19F NMR (235 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) -78.7 (d, J
= 6.5 Hz, 3F); IR (neat) 2961, 2904, 2841, 1614, 1588, 1515, 1465, 1444
cm-1 ; HRMS (EI) calcd for [(C12H17F3O2Si)] 278.0950, found 278.0950.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on catalyst, optimized on solvent,
optimized on stoichiometry of ligand, optimized on ligand, optimized on
stoichiometry of catalyst, alternative reaction conditions shown, Schlenk
tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Fe-Catalyzed Nucleophilic Activation of C-Si versus Allylic C-O Bonds:
Catalytic Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl Groups versus Tandem
Trifluormethylation-Allylation of Olefins
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Klein, Johannes E. M. N.; Rommel, Susanne; Plietker, Bernd
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organometallics (2014), 33(20), 5802-5810

