$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To benzaldehyde (0.53 g, 5.0 mmol) in a dry
flask under N2 were added DMF (anhydrous, 5 mL), TMSCF3 (2.0 g, 14.0
mmol), and carbene (8.5 mg, 0.025 mmol).The mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 45 min. HCl solution (2 N, 5 mL) was added and the
solution was stirred at room temperature until all TMS
protectedintermediate converted to product. Water (30 mL) was added and
the aqueous layer was extracted with ether (20 mLx3). Organic layers were
combined and washed with saturated NaHC03 aqueous solution (1 5 mL),
brine (1 5 mL), dried over MgS04. Solvents were removed under vacuum to
give the crude residue, which was purified by silica flash chromatography
(30% ethyl acetatehexanes) to give product of 1H NMR (CDC13, 400 MHz) δ
7.48 (m, 2H), 7.41 (m, 3H), 5.03 (q, J = 3.04 Hz, lH),2.52 (d, J= 4.04
Hz, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study ; optimized on catalyst and solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl
Compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
