$DATUM 107-12-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Iododifluoromethylation of aldehydes (General
procedure). Lithium iodide monohydrate (38 mg, 0.25 mmol) was dried by
heating with the heat gun (ca. 300 °C) under vacuum of oil pump during 3
min, and the flask was cooled to room temperature and filled with argon.
Propionitrile (1 mL), Bu4NI (203 mg, 0.55 mmol), aldehyde 2 (0.5 mmol),
and silane 1b (375 mg, 1.5 mmol) were successively added, and the
reaction mixture was heated under gentle reflux for 10 hours. The dark
brown mixture was cooled to room temperature, trifluoroacetic acid (154
μL, 2 mmol) and KHF2 (78 mg, 1 mmol) were added, and the mixture was
stirred for 1 h at room temperature. For the work-up, saturated aqueous
Na2CO3 (1 mL) was added dropwise followed by addition of water (5 mL),
and the mixture was extracted with methyl tert-butyl ether (3×3 mL). The
combined organic phases were washed with aqueous Na2S2O3 (10 mL, 0.1 M),
filtered through Na2SO4, and concentrated under vacuum. The residue was
dissolved in small amount of hexane/EtOAc (2/1), passed through short (1
cm) silica gel pad washing with 5 mL of hexane/EtOAc (2/1). The solvent
was evaporated, and the residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel. 2,2-Difluoro-2-iodo-1-phenylethanol (4m).
1-(4-Chlorophenyl)-2,2-difluoro-2-iodoethanol (4o). Yield 156 mg (98%).
Pale yellow oil. Chromatography hexanes/EtOAc 10 : 1 → 5 : 1. Rf 0.32
(hexanes/EtOAc 5 : 1). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3), δ: 3.18 (d, 1H, J = 3.3),
4.55–4.71 (m, 1H), 7.34–7.45 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3), δ: 79.3
(t, J = 24.1), 107.4 (dd, J = 319.5, 317.6), 128.7, 129.4 (t, J = 1.35),
133.0 (d, J = 3.3), 135.5. 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3), δ: –54.1 (dd, 1F, J
= 182.3, 9.6), –49.3 (dd, 1F, J = 182.3, 6.7). Calcd for C8H6ClF2IO
(318.49): C, 30.17; H, 1.90. Found: C, 30.03; H, 1.99.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nucleophilic Bromo- and Iododifluoromethylation of Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
