$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Trifluoromethyl Alcohols 3a-f.
General Method. To a solution of ketone 2 (2 mmol) and CsF (0.05 mmol) in
THF (50 mL), cooled to 0 °C, under argon was added dropwise a solution of
trifluoromethyltrimethylsilane (TMSCF3) in THF (1.5 mL, 3 mmol), and the
mixture was stirred at that temperature until the reaction was finished
(TLC). Subsequently, TBAF (2 mmol) was added, and the reaction mixture
was stirred for 1 h at room temperature. THF was removed under vacuum,
and the residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel using
hexanes-ethyl acetate 8:1 as eluent.
(1R,2'S,4a'S,7'R,8a'R)-1-(3-Benzyl-4',4',7'-trimethyloctahydro-
2H-benz[e][1,3]oxazin-2'-yl)-2,2,2-trifluoro-1-(furan-2-yl)ethanol (3c).
Yield: 96%. Yellow oil. [α]23 D +3.2 (c = 0.84, CHCl3). 1H NMR (δ): 0.70
(s, 3H); 0.71-1.05 (m, 2H); 0.95 (d, 3H, J = 6.5 Hz); 1.17 (q, 1H, J =
11.9 Hz); 1.32 (s, 3H); 1.51-1.73 (m, 4H); 1.96 (m, 1H); 3.73 (td, 1H, J
1 = 10.6 Hz, J 2 = 3.9 Hz); 3.77 (d, 1H, J = 17.6 Hz); 4.00 (br s, 1H);
4.49 (d, 1H, J = 17.6 Hz); 5.45 (s, 1H); 6.13 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 3.2 Hz, J 2
= 1.8 Hz), 6.20 (dd, 1H, J 1 = 3.2 Hz, J 2 = 0.8 Hz), 6.66 (dd, 2H, J 1 )
8.0 Hz, J 2 = 1.8 Hz); 6.98-7.24 (m, 3H); 7.41 (dd, 1H, J 1= 1.8 Hz, J 2
= 0.8 Hz). 19F NMR (δ): -79.1 (s, 3F). 13C NMR (δ): 22.2; 22.5; 24.7;
26.9; 31.4; 35.0; 41.1; 43.6; 47.4; 58.6; 78.0; 83.9; 110.1; 110.6;
125.1; 126.3 (2C); 127.2 (2C); 142.4; 143.6; 147.1. 13C NMR (acetone-d 6,
δ): 22.6; 23.0; 25.5; 27.5; 32.1; 35.8; 42.1; 44.4; 48.3; 59.4; 78.0 (q);
78.7; 85.1; 110.7; 111.4; 125.9; 127.4 (2C); 128.1 (2C); 143.6; 145.3;
149.6. IR (film): 3505; 3045; 3020; 1600; 1450; 1382; 1368; 1315; 1263;
1240; 1190; 730; 710; 690 cm-1. Anal. Calcd for C24H30F3NO3: C, 65.89; H,
6.91; N, 3.20. Found: C, 65.71; H, 7.06; N, 3.04.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Efficient Synthesis of Enantiomerically Enriched Trifluoromethylated
1,2-Diols and 1,2-Amino Alcohols with Quaternary Stereocenters by
Diastereoselective Addition of TMSCF3 to Chiral
2-Acyl-1,3-perhydrobenzoxazines
