$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Using 3a: To a stirred solution of 1a (30.0
mg, 0.18 mmol), 3a (10.5 mg, 0.018 mmol) and TMAF (3.3 mg, 0.035 mmol) in
toluene/CH2Cl2 (2/1, 0.5 mL) was added Me3SiCF3 (52.2 μL, 0.35 mmol) at -
80°C under N2 atmosphere. After reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h at
the same temperature, it was quenche-d with sat. NH4Cl aq. Aqueous layer
was extracted with AcOEt (5 mL x 2), and the combined organic layers was
washed with brine, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated under reduced
pressure to furnish the crude 2a as a trimethylsilyl ether. The
trimethylsilyl ether was treated with TBAF (50.6 mg, 0.19 mmol) in THF
(1.5 mL) at room temperature for 1h. The resulting mixture was
concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (acetone/n-hexane= 10/1) to give 2a (41.7
mg, 98%, 87% ee) as a white solid.
(R)-1,1,1-trifluoro-2-(3-nitrophenyl)propan-2-ol (2n) The reaction of 1n
(33.0 mg, 0.20 mmol) with Me3SiCF3 (59.1 μL, 0.40 mmol) catalyzed by TMAF
(1.9 mg, 0.02 mmol) and 3a (12.0 mg, 0.02 mmol) in toluene/CH2Cl2 (2/1,
0.5 mL) in presence of MS 4A (100 mg) gave 2n (45.1 mg, 96%, 64 % ee) as
pale yellow oil sup>1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.86 (s, 3H), 2.67 (br s, 1H), 7.59
(t, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.93 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 8.21.8.27 (m, 1H), 8.48
(s, 1H), 19F NMR (CDCl3) δ .81.1 (s, 3F); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 50.3 MHz) δ
23.9, 74.4 (q, J = 29.5 Hz), 121.4, 123.4, 124.8 (q, J = 284.5 Hz),
129.2, 132.3, 140.3, 147.8; IR (neat) 3495, 1534, 1348, 1285, 1169, 1091,
696 cm-1; MS (EI, m/z ) 235 (M+), 166; The ee of the product was
determined by HPLC using an OD-H column (n-hexane/i-PrOH = 95/5, flow
rate 0.5 mL/min, λ = 254 nm, τmaj =15.2 min, τmin = 18.7 min), [α]D25 =
+5.8 (c = 0.60 , CHCl3) , 64% ee.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 64% ee, molecular sieves used
