$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Experimental Procedures for
TBD-Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation with TMSCF3. Carbonyl compounds (1.0
mmol) and TMSCF3 (2.0 mmol) were added to a solution of TBD (0.05 mmol)
in DMF (2 mL) at room temperature. After the reaction was complete (as
determined by TLC), the resultant mixture was quenched with water (3 mL).
The mixture was extracted with Et2O, and the organic layer was washed
with brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and evaporated. The crude
mixture was purified by column chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc-hexane
= 1:9) to give the corresponding product.
[1-(4-Bromophenyl)-2,2,2-trifluoroethoxy]-trimethylsilane 2d. Yield 91%.
Carbonyl compound 1d, Time 30 min. 1H NMR (400 Hz, CDCl3) δ 0.08 (s, 9H),
4.85 (q, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 7.32 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 7.50 (d, J = 8.6 Hz,
1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ-0.3, 72.4 (q, 2J(C-F) = 32.4 Hz), 123.4,
124.1 (q, 1J(C-F) = 282.0 Hz), 129.0, 129.3, 134.5, 135.4.
