$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Trifluoromethyl Alcohols 3a-f.
General Method. To a solution of ketone 2 (2 mmol) and CsF (0.05 mmol) in
THF (50 mL), cooled to 0 °C, under argon was added dropwise a solution of
trifluoromethyltrimethylsilane (TMSCF3) in THF (1.5 mL, 3 mmol), and the
mixture was stirred at that temperature until the reaction was finished
(TLC). Subsequently, TBAF (2 mmol) was added, and the reaction mixture
was stirred for 1 h at room temperature. THF was removed under vacuum,
and the residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel using
hexanes-ethyl acetate 8:1 as eluent.
(2S,2'S,4a'S,7'R,8a'R)-2-(3-Benzyl-4',4',7'-trimethyloctahydro-
2H-benz[e][1,3]oxazin-2'-yl)-1,1,1-trifluoro-3-methylbutan-2- ol (3e).
Yield: 95%. White solid. Mp: 117-118 °C (from ethanol). [α]23 D +3.1 (c =
1.0, CHCl3). 1H NMR (δ): 0.84-1.00 (m, 5H); 0.84 (s, 3H); 0.95 (d, 3H, J
= 6.6 Hz); 1.08-1.20 (m, 4H); 1.32 (s, 3H); 1.40-1.71 (m, 4H); 1.93 (m,
1H); 2.22 (m, 1H); 3.55 (s, 1H); 3.63 (td, 1H, J 1 = 10.8 Hz, J 2 = 4.0
Hz); 3.94 (d, 1H, J = 18.3 Hz); 4.59 (d, 1H, J = 18.3 Hz); 5.02 (s, 1H);
7.15 (t, 1H, J = 7.1 Hz); 7.24-7.29 (m, 2H); 7.34 (d, 2H, J = 6.9 Hz).
19F NMR (δ): -71.7 (s, 3F). 13C NMR (δ): 16.4; 17.4; 22.2; 22.4; 24.8;
27.0; 30.1; 31.4; 35.1; 41.2; 43.5; 47.7; 59.1; 78.2; 79.1 (q, 2 J CF =
23.6 Hz); 84.4; 125.8; 126.3 (2C); 128.0 (2C); 143.9. IR (KBr): 3517;
3080; 1603; 1493; 1458; 1373; 1363; 1315; 1247; 1190; 1167; 779; 756;
719; 697 cm-1. Anal. Calcd for C23H34F3NO2: C, 66.80; H, 8.29; N, 3.39.
Found: C, 66.70; H, 8.19; N, 3.48.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, ether can also be used as solvent, TBAF as catalyst gave
lower stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Efficient Synthesis of Enantiomerically Enriched Trifluoromethylated
1,2-Diols and 1,2-Amino Alcohols with Quaternary Stereocenters by
Diastereoselective Addition of TMSCF3 to Chiral
2-Acyl-1,3-perhydrobenzoxazines
