$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Trifluoromethyl Alcohols 3a-f.
General Method. To a solution of ketone 2 (2 mmol) and CsF (0.05 mmol) in
THF (50 mL), cooled to 0 °C, under argon was added dropwise a solution of
trifluoromethyltrimethylsilane (TMSCF3) in THF (1.5 mL, 3 mmol), and the
mixture was stirred at that temperature until the reaction was finished
(TLC). Subsequently, TBAF (2 mmol) was added, and the reaction mixture
was stirred for 1 h at room temperature. THF was removed under vacuum,
and the residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel using
hexanes-ethyl acetate 8:1 as eluent.
(2S,2'S,4a'S,7'R,8a'R)-2-(3-Benzyl-4',4',7'-trimethyloctahydro-
2H-benz[e][1,3]oxazin-2’-yl)-1,1,1-trifluorohexan-2-ol (3f). Yield: 94%.
White solid. Mp: 108-109 °C (from methanol). [α]23 D +9.1 (c = 0.88,
CHCl3). 1H NMR (δ): 0.94-1.09 (m, 2H); 0.97 (t, 3H, J = 6.0 Hz); 0.97 (s,
3H); 1.03 (d, 3H, J = 6.5 Hz); 1.17- 1.38 (m, 4H), 1.42 (s, 3H);
1.59-1.80 (m, 7H); 2.02 (m, 1H); 3.55 (s, 1H); 3.72 (td, 1H, J 1 = 10.7
Hz, J 2 = 3.8 Hz); 4.04 (d, 1H, J = 18.4 Hz); 4.75 (d, 1H, J = 18.4 Hz);
5.06 (s, 1H); 7.23 (t, 1H, J = 7.3 Hz); 7.35 (t, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz); 7.46
(d, 2H, J = 7.3 Hz). 19F NMR (δ): -76.5 (s, 3F). 13C NMR (δ): 14.0; 22.2;
22.5; 23.0; 24.8; 25.0; 26.7; 31.3; 31.4; 35.1; 41.2; 43.6; 47.3; 58.8;
77.9; 83.8; 125.7; 126.4 (2C); 127.8 (2C); 143.6. IR (Nujol): 3545; 3080;
1600; 1490; 1450; 1375; 1315; 1180; 1160; 755; 725; 700 cm-1. Anal. Calcd
for C24H36F3NO2: C, 67.42; H, 8.49; N, 3.28. Found: C, 67.25; H, 8.36; N,
3.26.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, TBAF as catalyst gave lower stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Efficient Synthesis of Enantiomerically Enriched Trifluoromethylated
1,2-Diols and 1,2-Amino Alcohols with Quaternary Stereocenters by
Diastereoselective Addition of TMSCF3 to Chiral
2-Acyl-1,3-perhydrobenzoxazines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pedrosa, Rafael; Sayalero, Sonia; Vicente, Martina; Maestro, Alicia
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(5), 2177-2180

