$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedures for the
Trifluoromethylation of N-Benzoylaldohydrazones. Method A.
Allyltrimethylsilane (166 μL, 1.05 mmol) and BF3 · OEt2 (133 μL, 1.05
mmol) were successively added to a suspension of N-bezoylhydrazone (0.7
mmol) in 1,2-dichloroethane (1.4 mL), and the mixture was heated at
gentle reflux for 5 min. The solvent was evaporated in vacuum, the
residue was dissolved in DMF (1.4 mL) followed by addition of Me3SiCF3
(207 μL, 1.4 mmol) and NaOAc (230 mg, 2.8 mmol). The mixture was stirred
for 2 h at room temperature, quenched with 1 mL of saturated aqueous
Na2CO3, and stirred for additional 5 min. The mixture was diluted with
water (~10 mL) and extracted with ether (for 3a-c,e,g-k) or ethyl acetate
(for 3d,f) (4 × 4 mL). The combined organic phase was dried with Na2SO4,
concentrated, and the residue was flash chromatographed on silica gel.
N'-[2,2,2-trifluoro-1-(2-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]benzohydrazide (3c).
Chromatography: hexanes/EtOAc, 3 : 1, Rf = 0.30 (hexanes/EtOAc, 3 : 1).
M.p. 145-147 °C. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): 3.76 (s, 3H), 5.16-5.35 (m,
2H), 6.90 (d, 1H, J = 8.3), 6.99 (t, 1H, J = 7.6), 7.26-7.59 (m, 5H),
7.75 (d, 2H, J = 6.8), 8.17 (d, 1H, J = 5.9). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3):
55.5, 57.6 (q, J = 28.4), 110.9, 120.5, 125.3 (q, J = 282), 126.9, 128.4,
128.5, 130.4, 131.9, 132.2, 157.5, 167.3. 19 F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3):
-73.7 (d, J = 8.5). Calcd for C16H15F3N2O2 (324.30): C, 59.26; H, 4.66;
N, 8.64. Found: C, 59.37; H, 4.75; N, 8.61.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Ruppert-Prakash reagent used in stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Trifluoromethylation of N-Benzoylhydrazones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Dilman, Alexander D.; Arkhipov, Dmitry E.; Levin, Vitalij V.; Belyakov,
Pavel A.; Korlyukov, Alexander A.; Struchkova, Marina I.; Tartakovsky,
Vladimir A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2008), 73(14), 5643-5646

