$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the enantioselective
trifluoromethylation reaction of alkynyl ketones : To a stirred solution
of alkynyl ketone 1 (0.20 mmol), catalyst 3a (17.0 mg, 0.020 mmol, 10
mol%) and Me4NF (3.7 mg, 0.040 mmol, 0.2 equiv) in toluene/CH2Cl2 (2/1,
0.5 mL) was added Me3SiCF3 (59.1 μL, 0.40 mmol, 2.0 equiv) at −60°C under
nitrogen atmosphere. After reaction mixture was stirred at the same
temperature, it was quenched with sat. NH4Cl aq. Aqueous layer was
extracted with CH2Cl2, and the combined organic layers was washed with
brine, dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure to
furnish the crude 2 as a trimethylsilyl ether. The trimethylsilyl ether
was treated with nBu4NF [57.5 mg, 0.22 mmol, 1.1 equiv (in the cases of
substrates 1v or 1w, 2.2 equiv ofnBu4NF was uesd)] in THF (1.5 mL) at
room temperature for 1h. The resulting mixture was concentrated under
reduced pressure, and purified by column chromatography on silica gel
(n-hexane/acetone = 9/1) to give trifluoromethylated compounds (S)−2.
(S)-1,1,1-Trifluoro-5,5-dimethyl-2-phenylhex-3-yn-2-ol (2e)
(S)-5-(Benzyloxy)-1,1,1-trifluoro-5-methyl-2-(naphthalen-3-yl)hex-3-yn-2-ol
)(2r) Reaction of 1r (65.7 mg, 0.20 mmol), Me3SiCF3 (59.1 μL, 0.40 mmol,
2.0 equiv), catalyst 3a (17.0 mg, 0.020 mmol), Me4NF (3.7 mg, 0.040 mmol,
0.2 equiv) in toluene/CH2Cl2 (2/1, 0.5 mL) at -60 °C for 2 h. A Single
recrystallization of 2r (83% ee) from hexane/CH2Cl2 afforded 99% ee of
2r. 2r (74.1 mg, 93%, 83% ee) as a white solid. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ
1.64 (s, 6H), 2.99 (s, 1H), 4.69 (s, 2H), 7.27-7.38 (m, 5H), 7.51-7.54
(m, 2H), 7.78 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.82-7.88 (m, 2H), 8.21 (s, 1H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 150.9 MHz) δ 28.5, 28.6, 67.0, 70.7, 73.0 (q, J = 32.2 Hz),
80.2, 91.1, 123.4 (q, J = 285.7 Hz), 124.1, 126.5, 126.97, 127.02,
127.56, 127.58, 127.7, 128.0, 128.4, 128.6, 132.4, 132.6, 133.6, 138.6;
19F NMR (CDCl3, 282 MHz) δ -80.7 (s, 3F); IR (KBr) 3317, 3033, 2987,
2939, 2244, 1508, 1455, 1383, 1361, 1245, 1183, 1154, 1123, 1035, 930,
814, 743 cm-1 ; mp = 106.0-107.0 ºC; MS (ESI, m/z) 421 [(M+Na)+ ], HRMS
(ESI) calcd. for C24H21F3NaO2 [(M+Na)+ ]: 421.1391 Found: 421.1392 ; The
ee of the product was determined by HPLC using an AD-3 column
(n-hexane/i-PrOH = 95/5, flow rate 0.5 mL/min, λ = 254 nm, τmaj = 22.8
min, τmin = 25.7 min); [α]D 25 = -2.8 (c = 1.36, CHCl3) , 99% ee.
