$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Trifluoromethyl Alcohols 3a-f.
General Method. To a solution of ketone 2 (2 mmol) and CsF (0.05 mmol) in
THF (50 mL), cooled to 0 °C, under argon was added dropwise a solution of
trifluoromethyltrimethylsilane (TMSCF3) in THF (1.5 mL, 3 mmol), and the
mixture was stirred at that temperature until the reaction was finished
(TLC). Subsequently, TBAF (2 mmol) was added, and the reaction mixture
was stirred for 1 h at room temperature. THF was removed under vacuum,
and the residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel using
hexanes-ethyl acetate 8:1 as eluent.
(1S,2'S,4a'S,7'R,8a'R)-1-(3-Benzyl-4',4',7'-trimethyloctahydro-
2H-benz[e][1,3]oxazin-2'-yl)-2,2,2-trifluoro-1-(4-methoxyphenyl)- ethanol
(3b). Yield: 93%. White solid. Mp: 184-185 °C (from ethanol). [α]23 D
+7.1 (c = 1.0, CHCl3). 1H NMR (δ): 0.68 (s, 3H); 0.93-1.00 (m, 2H); 0.97
(d, 3H, J = 6.4 Hz); 1.18 (q, 1H, J = 11.7 Hz); 1.34 (s, 3H); 1.50-1.75
(m, 4H); 2.01 (m, 1H); 3.67 (d, 1H, J = 17.6 Hz); 3.75 (s, 3H); 3.76 (td,
1H, J 1 = 10.6 Hz, J 2 = 4.0 Hz); 4.14 (s, 1H); 4.37 (d, 1H, J = 17.6
Hz); 5.48 (s, 1H); 6.40-6.42 (m, 2H); 6.72 (m, 2H); 6.87-7.28 (m, 3H);
7.33 (d, 2H, J = 8.5 Hz). 19F NMR (δ): -78.8 (s, 3F). 13C NMR (δ): 22.2;
22.4; 24.8; 27.1; 31.4; 35.1; 41.2; 43.6; 47.1; 55.1; 58.6; 78.0; 78.3
(q, 2 J CF = 26.5 Hz); 84.9; 113.2; 124.9; 126.0; 127.1; 128.3 (9C);
125.7; 143.4; 159.6 (3C). IR (KBr): 3521; 3086; 3058; 1615; 1586; 1516;
1462; 1388; 1376; 1314; 1299; 1251; 939; 834; 804; 756; 701 cm-1. MS
(m/z): 478 (M + 1, 100), 324 (38), 272 (66). Anal. Calcd for C27H34F3NO3:
C, 67.91; H, 7.18; N, 2.93. Found: C, 67.76; H, 6.99; N, 2.98.
