$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Iododifluoromethylation of aldehydes (General procedure). Lithium iodide
monohydrate (38 mg, 0.25 mmol) was dried by heating with the heat gun
(ca. 300 °C) under vacuum of oil pump during 3 min, and the flask was
cooled to room temperature and filled with argon. Propionitrile (1 mL),
Bu4NI (203 mg, 0.55 mmol), aldehyde 2 (0.5 mmol), and silane 1b (375 mg,
1.5 mmol) were successively added, and the reaction mixture was heated
under gentle reflux for 10 hours. The dark brown mixture was cooled to
room temperature, trifluoroacetic acid (154 μL, 2 mmol) and KHF2 (78 mg,
1 mmol) were added, and the mixture was stirred for 1 h at room
temperature. For the work-up, saturated aqueous Na2CO3 (1 mL) was added
dropwise followed by addition of water (5 mL), and the mixture was
extracted with methyl tert-butyl ether (3×3 mL). The combined organic
phases were washed with aqueous Na2S2O3 (10 mL, 0.1 M), filtered through
Na2SO4, and concentrated under vacuum. The residue was dissolved in small
amount of hexane/EtOAc (2/1), passed through short (1 cm) silica gel pad
washing with 5 mL of hexane/EtOAc (2/1). The solvent was evaporated, and
the residue was purified by column chromatography on silica gel.
2,2-Difluoro-2-iodo-1-phenylethanol (4m). Yield 131 mg (92%). Pale yellow
oil. Chromatography hexanes/EtOAc 10 : 1 → 5 : 1. Rf 0.4 (hexanes/EtOAc 5
: 1). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3), δ: 3.08 (s, 1H), 4.69 (t, 1H, J = 9.9),
7.39–7.53 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3), δ: 80.1 (t, 1H, J = 23.6),
107.8 (dd, J = 320.2, 317.9), 128.1, 128.5, 129.5, 134.7 (d, J = 2.3).
19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3), δ: –53.7 (dd, 1F, J = 180.1, 9.9), –48.9 (dd,
1F, J = 180.1, 9.9). Calcd for C8H7F2IO (284.04): C, 33.83; H, 2.48.
Found: C, 33.79; H, 2.49.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
