$DATUM (R)-2-[2'-(Diphenylphosphoryl)-1,1'-binaphthyl-2-yl]-1,1,1,3,3,3-hexafluoropropan-2-ol
((R)-4) To a mixture of (R)-3 (830 mg, 1.5 mmol) and CsF (67 mg, 0.45
mmol) in anhydrous benzonitrile (3.5 mL) was added
trimethyl(trifluoromethyl)silane (528 mg, 1.5 mmol) dropwise at 0 °C.
Then, the reaction mixture was warmed to room temperature with stirring.
During the reaction, CF3SiMe3 (528 mg, 1.5 mmol) was added to the mixture
after stirring for 4 h. And after 8 hours, further addition of CF3SiMe3
(528 mg, 1.5 mmol) to the reaction mixture was executed. Thus, the
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for total 24 h. After
removal of PhCN by Kugelrohr distillation in vacuo, the residue was
dissolved in THF (20 mL). To the solution was added 4N hydrochloric acid
(20 mL) was added and then the mixture was stirred at room temperature
for 12 h. Organic materials were extracted for three times with ethyl
acetate and the combined organic layer were washed with brine and dried
over Na2SO4. After removal of the solvent under reduced pressure, the
residue was purified by silica-gel column chromatography (hexane/ethyl
acetate, 3/1) to give (R)-4 (836 mg, 1.35 mmol, 90%) as pale yellow
solids;
(R)-2-[2'-(Diphenylphosphoryl)-1,1'-binaphthyl-2-yl]-1,1,1,3,3,3-hexafluoropropan-2-ol
((R)-4), yield 836 mg, 1.35 mmol, 90%. mp 202-203 °C; [α]D25 = +26.1 (c
0.80, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9 .54 (1H, s), 7.95-7.86 (4H, m),
7.78 (1H, d, J = 9.2 Hz), 7.68 (1H, d, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.60-7.49 (5H, m),
7.40 (1H, dd, 3JHP = 12.8 Hz, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.22 (1H, t, J = 8.0 Hz),
7.18-7.11 (3H, m), 6.93-6.83 (3H, m), 6.70- 6.63 (2H, m), 6.34 (1H, d, J
= 8.8 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) 144.68 (d, 3JCF = 7.4 Hz), 135.1,
135.0, 134.83, 134.3 (d, 1JCP = 99 Hz), 133.2 (d, 3JCP = 11.5 Hz), 132.4,
132.3, 132.2, 132,1. 130.9, 130.6 (d, 2JCP = 10 Hz), 130.6, 129.9 (d,
2JCP = 10 Hz), 128.9, 128.8, 128.7, 128.1, 128.0, 127.9, 127.7, 127.6,
127.5, 127.4, 127.2, 127.1, 127.0, 126.7, 126.5, 126.1, 124.3 (q, 1JCF =
290 Hz), 122.7 (q, 1JCF = 287 Hz), 81.6 (sept, 2JCF = 29 Hz); 19F NMR
(376 MHz, CDCl3) δ 94.0 (3F, q, 4JFF = 7.5 Hz), 87.5 (3F,q, 4JFF = 7.5
Hz); ESI-MS m/z (%) 621 (M+H+, 100). Anal. Calcd for C35H23F6O2P: 67.75;
H, 3.74. Found: C, 67.56; H, 3.91.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition
