$DATUM This compound was prepared using 2-formyl thiophen-3-yl boronic acid (156
mg, 1.0 mmol), 2-bromo-furan (145 mg, 1.0 mmol), aqueous sodium carbonate
(1M, 2 mL), and dichlorobis(triphenylphosphine) palladium(II) (50 mg,
0.071 mmol) by following a similar procedure described for 1a to provide
the crude material which was purified by silica gel column chromatography
to afford the titled compound (162 mg, 95% ) for immediate use in next
step. MS (EI) m/z: 179
2,2,2-trifluoro-1-(3-(furan-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)-ethanol. This compound
was prepared using tetrabutylammonium fluoride (0.1 mL, 1M in THF),
3-(furan-2-yl)thiophene-2-carbaldehyde (178 mg, 1 mmol) and
trifluoromethyl trimethylsilane (0.2 mL, 1.2 mmol), by following a
similar procedure described for 10m to give 0.180 g (90 %) of the crude
titled compound which was directly used in next step.
