$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To aldehyde (0.52 g, 4.1 mmol) in a dry flask under N2 were added DMF
(anhydrous, 5 mL)and TMSCF3 (1.7 g, 12.2 mmol). After the mixture was
cooled to -25 °C, carbene 1 (7mg, 0.021 mmol, 0.005 eq) was added. The
mixture was warmed to room temperature and stirred at that temperature
for 1 h. A 2N HCl solution (6 mL) was added and thesolution was stirred
at room temperature until all TMS protected intermediate convertedto
product. Water (30 mL) was added and the aqueous layer was extracted with
ether (2x20 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with saturated
NaHC03 aqueoussolution (15 mL), brine (15 mL), and dried over MgS04.
Solvents were removed undervacuum to give the crude residue, which was
purified by silica flash chromatography (1 0% to 30% ethyl acetate in
hexanes) to give yield 0.73 g,90%. 1H NMR (CDC13, 400 MHz) δ 3.85-3.99
(m, lH), 1.90-2.15 (brs, lH), 1.5 1-1.80 (m, 2H),1.20-1.50 (m, lOH), 0.91
(t, J = 8.00 Hz, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Heterocyclic Carbene Catalyzed Trifluoromethylation of Carbonyl
Compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Song, Jinhua J.; Tan, Zhulin; Reeves, Jonathan T.; Gallou, Fabrice; Yee,
Nathan K.; Senanayake, Chris H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2005), 7(11), 2193-2196

